@startuml
title Student Feature — Class Diagram (Specify)
hide methods
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class Session
class Team
class Participant {
  identity: activity-scoped, server-verified
  recovery: same browser
}
class Round {
  phase: Waiting | Active | Ended
}
class Question
class Blank
class QuestionGroup
class Submission {
  acceptedOrder: server-assigned
}
class SubmissionAnswer
class Result
class SessionStateSnapshot
class TeamAnswerDraft {
  scope: one Team + one Round
  storage: Student Feature server
  conflict: last accepted edit wins
  after submission: read-only
}
class DraftAnswer

Session "1" -- "0..*" Team : contains
Session "1" -- "0..*" Round : has attempts
Team "1" -- "0..*" Participant : members
Team "1" -- "0..*" Submission : submits
Round "1" -- "0..*" Submission : receives
Round "0..*" --> "1" Question : targets one
Round "0..*" --> "1" QuestionGroup : or targets one
Question "1" *-- "0..*" Blank : independent answers
QuestionGroup "0..1" -- "0..*" Question : groups questions
Submission "1" *-- "0..*" SubmissionAnswer : stores
SubmissionAnswer "0..*" --> "1" Blank : answers
Round "1" -- "0..1" Result : publishes when ended
Result "0..*" --> "1" Submission : winning submission
SessionStateSnapshot ..> Session : phase / version / target reference
TeamAnswerDraft ..> Participant : edited by team members
Team "1" -- "0..*" TeamAnswerDraft : drafts
Round "1" -- "0..*" TeamAnswerDraft : drafts
TeamAnswerDraft "1" *-- "0..*" DraftAnswer : stores current values
DraftAnswer "0..*" --> "1" Blank : answers

note right of Team
Only the first joined Participant is the confirmed
group leader, chosen atomically by the server.
Transient disconnect preserves leadership. A pre-start
team change requires explicit handoff; an unrecoverable
leader requires authorized Teacher transfer.
end note

note right of Participant
No reusable student account/password.
Server creates and restores the activity identity;
credential mechanics remain for Plan.
end note

note bottom of QuestionGroup
QuestionGroup is a multi-Question target.
It is distinct from one Question with many Blanks.
Empty groups cannot be Round targets.
end note

note right of Result
After Ended, Student sees only the winning Team name
and its accepted answers. Student Feature selects the
earliest accepted Submission and supplies a student-only
result projection. Teacher hands that winner to Foundation's
existing End transaction; no public contract change.
end note

note bottom of TeamAnswerDraft
Student Feature server stores and immediately shares the draft;
the last server-accepted edit for a Blank is current. Every Blank
must be complete before submit; after accepted submission the draft
is read-only. Exact storage and protocol remain for Plan; Foundation
state events carry no draft answers.
end note
@enduml
